Dear all
=20
This is my very first post on a public mailing list where I am not into pro=
gramming.  I just set up and configure Linux but have very little experienc=
e with programing except BASIC and shell scripting.
=20
I have recently assembled a Linux server and router (no GUI) where I am usi=
ng an Atheros AR9160 controller (Sparklan WMIA-268N) as an access point.  I=
 am using Ubuntu 9.04 jaunty release but using hostapd 0.69 from the upcomi=
ng 9.10 karmic release because the one that comes with jaunty does not supp=
ort nl80211.
=20
The problem is that I am constantly getting kernel panics=2C each time of t=
he same error kernel panic ieee80211_agg_splice_packets+0x3d/0xc0 [mac80211=
]
=20
I have tried many compat-wireless releases including 2.6.31-rc*=2C daily bu=
ilds and many kernels including 2.6.31-* all to no avail=2C even the latest=
 one doesn't fix the problem.  The one which I have took screenshots is fro=
m kernel 2.6.28-13 with compat-wireless 2.6.30 installed.
=20
My easiest way to reproduce the problem is to surf the web using my Windows=
 notebook=2C turn wifi off using the button so that it is suddenly disconne=
cted without de-authenticating=2C turning wifi back on and then surfing the=
 web and this kernel panic comes just about every time.  The notebook is fi=
tted with an Intel 4965AGN in 802.11n mode where I have used both XP and Vi=
sta.
=20
I enclose screenshots of 3 occurrences=2C the last occurrence with the opti=
ons nosmp noacpi acpi=3Doff noapic just to see if it solves the problem but=
 it didn't.  Most frustratingly=2C I hate it when I am the only person expe=
riencing it because searching Google yields nothing with this error.
=20
Jack
